('shared_kernel/llm_payload.py',541,'Composite turn metadata normalizes typed fields and enforces supported roles/kinds/schema/family, None authority, bounded budgets/content length/canonical size and exact reply-field tuple for consequential turns. Kill-condition labels are sorted/deduplicated, not executed. from_dict checks exact builtin wire types, unknown/missing fields and conflicting legacy aliases; create instead silently prioritizes prompt aliases and supplies all-zero content digest/zero length when absent. Payload has no body, so content binding remains caller responsibility. payload_id hashes full serialized metadata; turn_manifest_root intentionally omits budgets/task/kill/length and declared domain constants are not used as hash prefixes. Labels IndependentHostEvaluationRequired/ReplayableLabEvidence do not perform verification. Factory and wire admission have materially different strictness.'),
('rewriting/__init__.py',62,'Explicit lazy dispatch/export table for boundary parser, byte partition receipts, containment and wire AST; caches attributes. No source-body, semantic or grammar proof is supplied by exports.'),
('rewriting/rewrites.py',150,'Bounded recursive parser admits lowercase/digit atoms or nonempty child lists, refuses mixed atoms/children and <> explicitly, limits root-depth32 and4096nodes/65536UTF8bytes. Bare Boundary constructor can render inadmissible empty/mixed trees. Segment checks only boundary syntax; bindings/request do not prove source coverage or role meaning, and authority fields are unrestricted strings. RewriteReceipt does not parse its root, compute its digest or bind count/content; TrialObservation uses coercible bool/float and is a claimed observation, not an independent trial. This parser grammar is narrower than an MSS-N prose grammar allowing empty boundaries.'),
('rewriting/rewriting_types.py',167,'Strict frozen models prove integer contiguous nonempty span coverage, prompt SHA256/UTF8 length, one sequential symbol per span and exact substring byte reconstruction. BoundaryWire regex allows any lowercase role letter and validates only sequential symbol numbers; CompilationReceipt never relates those letters to SpanRole, so byte preservation is not semantic role preservation. Standalone SymbolBinding lacks end>start/text-range checks but receipt supplies range/text binding. No prompt/number-of-spans resource budget. Regex match dollar anchor permits trailing newline on BoundaryWire. Role assignment is an admitted annotation, not a theorem about natural language.'),
('rewriting/wires.py',118,'Recursive Void/Atom/App models and profile/legend records are passive and mutable. WireCodec is a shallow whitespace splitter: nested application renders parse into Atom tokens rather than recursive trees, and Atom text has no escaping, so serialization is noninjective (Atom value () and Void both render ()). SyntaxProfile budgets/token restrictions and authority None are not enforced on WirePacket; grammar names are not semantic decoding proofs.'),
('rewriting/prompt_containment.py',81,'Frozen finite tree checks cardinality=1+sum(child cardinalities) and depth<=5 with literal None authority. This is occurrence-count tree bookkeeping, not semantic decomposition/containment of prompt tasks. Reused child objects count repeatedly and prompt refs need not be unique; no breadth/node budget. MutationKind/PipelineStage only labels, no pipeline ordering enforced.'),
('aggregates/rewriting_aggregate.py',66,'Checks first/last bounds and pairwise endpoint adjacency, including empty zero-length partition. Assumes ByteSpanVO/SpanRoleVO validity without runtime type checks; mutable aggregate can later drift. No source bytes, UTF8 boundaries or semantic roles are verified. from_pairs freezes outer sequence only.'),
